WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.435
Modern organizations generate enormous amounts of security-relevant information.

00:00:04.435 --> 00:00:09.150
Firewalls, servers, cloud platforms, endpoint tools, identity providers, applications,

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:11.160
and network devices all produce logs.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.865
Each source can tell part of the story,

00:00:12.865 --> 00:00:15.325
but none of them gives complete visibility by itself.

00:00:15.325 --> 00:00:17.850
Reviewing these logs manually is nearly impossible.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:21.358
Important warning signs may be buried among millions of normal events.

00:00:21.358 --> 00:00:24.200
A suspicious login, firewall deny, endpoint alert,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.960
and cloud configuration change may matter more when viewed together than when reviewed

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:28.534
separately.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:31.025
SIEM platforms help organizations collect, organize,

00:00:31.025 --> 00:00:35.640
and analyze this information so security teams can identify suspicious activity more

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.196
effectively.

00:00:36.196 --> 00:00:41.495
SIEM exists because defenders need visibility across many systems rather than isolated

00:00:41.495 --> 00:00:41.840
pieces of information.
